---
const moves = [
  "The conversation, every message of it",
  "Files Claude saved alongside it, like subagent transcripts",
  "Claude's memory for that folder",
];
const stays = [
  "Anything you do after the handoff. The copy is its own fork.",
  "The undo history for file edits, so rewind can't reach before the handoff",
  "Your other conversations, unless you hand them over too",
];
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 pb-24 sm:px-8">
  <div class="reveal max-w-xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-[0.75rem] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-muted">Handoff</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-[2rem] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] sm:text-[2.4rem]">
      Exactly what moves, and what stays.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="reveal rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h3 class="font-mono text-[0.8rem] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink">Copied</h3>
      <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3.5">
        {moves.map((item) => (
          <li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            <svg class="mt-1.5 h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0 text-ink" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3L13 4.5" /></svg>
            {item}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal rounded-2xl border border-line p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h3 class="font-mono text-[0.8rem] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-muted">Not copied</h3>
      <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3.5">
        {stays.map((item) => (
          <li class="flex gap-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
            <svg class="mt-1.5 h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 8h8" /></svg>
            {item}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="reveal mt-6 max-w-3xl text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Handing a conversation to another account means it's processed under that account's organization. ccswap names the
    organization and asks before it copies. If your workplace doesn't allow moving work between accounts, don't.
  </p>
</section>
